{
  "$comment": "Campaign level 40 (chapter 4, The Wild Heart): the first three tribe map of the chapter. A broad river valley: the player's meadow fills the middle of the north bank; the eastern tribe (tribe 1, aggressive) lives across a deep stream to the east; the western raiders (tribe 2, sneaky) camp on the far (south) bank in the west; a ford in the east joins the eastern land to the far bank. Neither rival can reach the player on foot, so every attack on the player is a scripted landing. Until the kill stage is done, scripted feud bands of both rivals (3 eastern wardens against 3 raider wardens and a firecaller) clash every 200 s on the far bank below the island. Stages: grow to ten followers and raise a Warden Lodge (until then eastern scouts land in the hills from 300 s every 200 s: the idle loss); kill twelve raiders (after it, raider bands of 4 land every 150 s on two alternating prongs, the western shallows and the north western hills, until it is done); take the seer stone on the river island (dormant until then, posted eastern guards, a raider band comes to pray it); the seer raises the raiders' old ford from the island to the far bank, so burn the raiders' Hearth past its posted guard and the feud survivors; that raises the eastern stream ford, the eastern tribe sends a war band, and the player burns the eastern Hearth past its posted guard and towers. Every home troop of tribe 1 is posted and both rivals start above maxTroops, so their only free troops are feud survivors (too few for a natural wave in the bot runs); maxPopulation caps their villages.",
